## Selected paintings

The `/paintings` page contains a manually curated personal selection of artworks. Reproduction sources are drawn from Wikimedia Commons and retained under `assets/sources/paintings`; quality-95 WebP derivatives are generated into the public site at build time. Neither the sources nor the generated images are covered by this repository's MIT or CC BY 4.0 grants. The site maintains source and licence links for each reproduced painting.

The page records a source and rights statement for every reproduced image. Most current reproductions are marked Public Domain on Wikimedia Commons. The reproduction used for Francisco de Goya's `Saturno` is credited as CC BY-SA 4.0 and is visibly credited on the page to Museo Nacional del Prado via Wikimedia Commons.

Leonora Carrington's `Las distracciones de Dagoberto` and Matthew Wong's `A Walk through Primordial Garden` are intentionally not reproduced because the artworks remain protected by copyright and no suitable republication licences have been identified. Pablo Picasso's `L'étagère` is also not reproduced: ALBERTINA explicitly credits its image to Succession Picasso / Bildrecht Wien. The page links to the relevant institutional records instead.

